# Shizuku starts the user service in a separate, shell-privileged process and resolves it by the
# class name Dizdar hands over in UserServiceArgs. R8 would otherwise rename or strip it, and the
# failure only shows up at provisioning time on a real device.
-keep class org.tamodak.dizdar.admin.provisioning.DizdarPrivilegedService { *; }

# Both ends of the binder call live in this APK, but the AIDL stub is matched by its descriptor
# string and fixed transaction ids — including destroy() = 16777114, which Shizuku itself calls.
-keep interface org.tamodak.dizdar.admin.provisioning.IDizdarPrivilegedService { *; }
-keep class org.tamodak.dizdar.admin.provisioning.IDizdarPrivilegedService$* { *; }
